From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] storage: Read the T8010's phy-ip window again

The S8000 change made reading the phy-ip register depend on has_phy_ip,
which it set for the S8003 only. The T8010 programs lane 0 through that
window as well (program_phy_lane0 in t8010_setup_link), so phy_ip_base
stayed 0 there: starting the internal storage wrote to address 0 and
m1n1 crashed, and the iPad 6 and 7 fell back to iOS when launched from
storage. Set has_phy_ip for the T8010.

Fixes: storage: Read NVMe on the S8000 (Samsung A9)
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 src/apcie_nvme.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/src/apcie_nvme.c
+++ b/src/apcie_nvme.c
@@ -783,6 +783,8 @@
         .compatible = "apcie,t8010",
         .setup_common = t8010_setup_common,
         .setup_link = t8010_setup_link,
+        /* t8010_setup_link programs lane 0 through the phy-ip window */
+        .has_phy_ip = true,
         .l1ss_ctl1 = 0x40550000,
         .nvmmu_init_busy = NVMMU_TCB_CTRL_BUSY,
         /* pinctrl-apple-gpio direction_output; also clears INPUT_ENABLE */
